    "sc_22_5_930_drug||How the \u00a7 22-5-930(A) route interacts with \u00a7 44-53-450(b) for a participant who would now be eligible for a conditional discharge. Subsection (A) was read at source on 2026-08-06 and expressly includes 'those charges for which the person would now be eligible for a conditional discharge pursuant to Section 44-53-450', which brings some conditional-discharge-type facts inside the conviction route; subsection (D) separately bars the route where the person actually had a conditional discharge within the lookback period. Which route a participant with both features should be pointed to, and in what order, is a counselling question the statute does not answer.": "Q-040",
    "sc_34_11_90e_check||The single-incident fee. Section 17-22-940(G) as amended by 2018 Act No. 254 was read at source on 2026-08-06 and provides that where multiple charges from a single incident are combined under \u00a7 17-1-40 or \u00a7 17-22-150(a), 'only one two hundred fifty-dollar fee, one twenty-five dollar SLED verification fee, and one thirty-five dollar clerk of court filing fee may be charged'. The controlling review reports the single-incident solicitor fee as one hundred fifty dollars, drawn from Supreme Court expungement guidance. The current statutory figure is two hundred fifty dollars. The packet quotes the statutory figure and does not promise the lower one.": "Q-041",
